    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Quick answer",
      "body": "To add OneDrive to File Explorer, install or open the OneDrive app, sign in with your Microsoft account, and complete OneDrive Setup.",
      "durationInFrames": 319
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "What you need to check before you start",
      "body": "You need a Windows 10 or Windows 11 PC with an internet connection. You also need a Microsoft personal…",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer/02-search-onedrive-start-menu.webp",
        "width": 791,
        "height": 355
      },
      "durationInFrames": 366
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 1: Download and install OneDrive manually",
      "body": "Download OneDrive from the official OneDrive download page, then install the app.",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer/03-download-onedrive-manually.webp",
        "width": 878,
        "height": 324
      },
      "durationInFrames": 297
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 2: Sign in to OneDrive",
      "body": "When OneDrive Setup opens, enter your Microsoft account email address and select Sign in.",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer/04-onedrive-signin-page-login.webp",
        "width": 586,
        "height": 546
      },
      "durationInFrames": 309
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 3: Select your preferred OneDrive folder location",
      "body": "OneDrive Setup shows the location for your OneDrive folder. Select Next to use the default location.",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer/05-select-onedrive-sync-folder.webp",
        "width": 575,
        "height": 524
      },
      "durationInFrames": 355
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 4: Review Files On-Demand",
      "body": "OneDrive Setup explains Files On-Demand. This feature lets you see OneDrive files without downloading every file to your PC.",
      "durationInFrames": 319
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 5: Open OneDrive in File Explorer",
      "body": "Open File Explorer. Select the File Explorer icon on the taskbar or press Windows key + E. Look in the left panel for OneDrive.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
